From: Robine Wake <noreply@robine-wake.local>
Subject: [PATCH] src: pass -static to libtool, not to the compiler

-static in AM_CFLAGS is meant for libtool (build libbluealsad.la as a static
convenience library), but AM_CFLAGS also reaches the final bluealsad link,
where gcc turns it into a fully static link. That fails on toolchains that
only provide shared libdbus-1 ("attempted static link of dynamic object").
Declare it as the library's LDFLAGS instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/Makefile.am	2026-10-02 00:46:06
+++ b/src/Makefile.am	2026-10-02 00:46:06
@@ -171,9 +171,10 @@
 	@MPG123_CFLAGS@ \
 	@OPUS_CFLAGS@ \
 	@SBC_CFLAGS@ \
-	@SPANDSP_CFLAGS@ \
-	-static
+	@SPANDSP_CFLAGS@
 
+libbluealsad_la_LDFLAGS = -static
+
 libbluealsad_la_LIBADD = \
 	shared/libshared.la \
 	@AAC_LIBS@ \
